nged voter set. The selected requirement is the public proposal-admission contract; inconsistent committed decisions or broader consensus safety would require separate evidence.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"src_node_application_contract\",\n      \"src_usage\",\n      \"src_readme_ready\",\n      \"src_membership_contract\",\n      \"src_node_status_apply\",\n      \"src_node_duplicate_config_test\",\n      \"src_node_learner_config_test\",\n      \"src_raw_entry\",\n      \"src_ready_accept\",\n      \"src_ready_contract\",\n      \"src_log_delivery\",\n      \"src_log_frontiers\",\n      \"src_raw_advance\",\n      \"src_applied\",\n      \"src_step\",\n      \"src_node_loop\",\n      \"src_leader_proposal\",\n      \"src_reset\",\n      \"src_election\",\n      \"src_replication\",\n      \"src_node_restart\",\n      \"src_node_propose_wait\",\n      \"src_cfg_activation\",\n      \"src_changer\",\n      \"src_restore_config\",\n      \"src_transfer_roles\",\n      \"src_tracker\",\n      \"src_majority\",\n      \"src_quorum_joint\",\n      \"src_startup\",\n      \"src_snapshot_restore\",\n      \"src_log_commit\",\n      \"src_append_success\",\n      \"src_log_recover\",\n      \"src_log_restore\",\n      \"src_unstable_replace\",\n      \"src_bootstrap\"\n    ],\n    \"participants\": [\n      \"Public Node caller\",\n      \"Serialized leader Node\",\n      \"Absent newly proposed voters\"\n    ],\n    \"objects\": [\n      \"Runtime application-progress acknowledgment\",\n      \"Prior committed configuration entry\",\n      \"Subsequent configuration proposal\",\n      \"Active tracker configuration\"\n    ],\n    \"contexts\": [\n      \"Synchronous Node with configuration validation enabled and no joint configuration\",\n      \"Persistence completed before Advance; actual configuration applications remain in Ready order\",\n      \"Finite deferral of first configuration activation, without rejecting it; no crash or role change during proposal interval\"\n    ],\n    \"event_paths\": [\n      \"Actual Campaign and first ProposeConfChange -> committed Ready -> completed persistence -> Node.Advance -> queued MsgStorageApplyResp -> internal applied acknowledgment\",\n      \"Second Node.ProposeConfChange -> stepLeader pendingConfIndex guard -> emitted configuration entry or dropped/replaced proposal\",\n      \"Later ApplyConfChange first, then subsequent committed configuration entries in order\"\n    ],\n    \"activity_classes\": [\n      \"A1\",\n      \"A5\",\n      \"A4\",\n      \"A7\"\n    ],\n    \"behavior_ids\": [\n      \"B_READY\",\n      \"B_PROPOSE\"\n    ],\n    \"fact_ids\": [\n      \"F_APPLIED_ACK\"\n    ],\n    \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n      \"B_NODE_OWNER\": \"Serializes public Node calls, which have the early-Advance permission selected for this question.\",\n      \"B_CONFIG\": \"ApplyConfChange activates membership separately from the acknowledged application frontier; returned calls distinguish activation from bookkeeping.\",\n      \"B_ELECT\": \"Produces the actual initial leader through Campaign and voting, not assigned role state.\",\n      \"B_COMMIT\": \"Produces the first committed configuration and exposes it through Ready; later commitment is a consequence outside the selected admission requirement.\",\n      \"B_RECONSTRUCT\": \"RestartNode reconstructs the valid single-voter prefix from caller Storage.\"\n    },\n    \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n    \"counterevidence\": [\n      \"Node.ApplyConfChange says it must be called whenever a configuration change is observed; an immediate-before-Advance reading would exclude the delayed policy. The numbered Node usage steps instead explicitly allow Advance any time after persistence, before the configuration application step, and preserve order rather than requiring completion before Advance.\",\n      \"RawNode.Advance describes applied-and-saved progress, but the selected entry is Node; importing the stricter lower-level wording would erase the explicit Node permission.\",\n      \"The duplicate-node test activates before Advance; it does not test or forbid overlap. The learner test iterates Entries, so its scheduling is not normative evidence of committed-entry duties.\",\n      \"The pendingConfIndex guard protects callers withholding Advance; activating first changes membership and quorum requirements. These protections must remain as controls.\",\n      \"Exploration 6dab32606865456a91887dbe509c632f observed acceptance under early Advance but remains construction knowledge, not evidence for this new obligation.\"\n    ],\n    \"unknowns\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"trigger_rationale\": \"The explicit step-order permission provides a concrete applicability basis beyond the generic snapshot example. Fix the narrower proposal-admission requirement and test the actual Node path with an independent activation record, preserving the alternative immediate-duty interpretation for review.\"\n  },\n  \"status\": \"escalated\",\n  \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n  \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n  \"stop_reason\": \"Fix a public Node admission obligation grounded in the explicit step-order permission and no-prior-unapplied-change promise, while preserving the narrower caller-duty interpretation for review. The formal endpoint is proposal encoding/admission, not general consensus safety.\",\n  \"resume_conditions\": [],\n  \"obligation_id\": \"C_PENDING_CONFIG_ADMISSION\",\n  \"result_claim_ids\": [\n    \"C_PENDING_CONFIG_ADMISSION\"\n  ],\n  \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n  \"current_applicability\": \"within_recorded_scope\",\n  \"executions\": [\n    {\n      \"check_id\": \"5f04338bd9e04060b57241324ec589da\",\n      \"artifact_id\": \"fd9efd7d132b4ed39389868a253233bb\",\n      \"action\": \"direct_check\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"outcome\": \"tests_passed\",\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"checks\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"5f04338bd9e04060b57241324ec589da\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"record\": {\n    \"path\": \"state.json\",\n    \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n    \"match\": {\n      \"id\": \"e90ce70ecaa74e3698ee914e1b646c30\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n973:func (r *raft) hup(t CampaignType) {\n983:\tif r.hasUnappliedConfChanges() {\n995:func (r *raft) hasUnappliedConfChanges() bool {\n1942:func (r *raft) promotable() bool {\n}\n\n// errBreak is a sentinel error used to break a callback-based loop.\nvar errBreak = errors.New(\"break\")\n\nfunc (r *raft) hasUnappliedConfChanges() bool {\n\tif r.raftLog.applied >= r.raftLog.committed { // in fact applied == committed\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfound := false\n\t// Scan all unapplied committed entries to find a config change. Paginate the\n\t// scan, to avoid a potentially unlimited memory spike.\n\tlo, hi := r.raftLog.applied+1, r.raftLog.committed+1\n\t// Reuse the maxApplyingEntsSize limit because it is used for similar purposes\n\t// (limiting the read of unapplied committed entries) when raft sends entries\n\t// via the Ready struct for application.\n\t// TODO(pavelkalinnikov): find a way to budget memory/bandwidth for this scan\n\t// outside the raft package.\n\tpageSize := r.raftLog.maxApplyingEntsSize\n\tif err := r.raftLog.scan(lo, hi, pageSize, func(ents []pb.Entry) error {\n\t\tfor i := range ents {\n\t\t\tif ents[i].Type == pb.EntryConfChange || ents[i].Type == pb.EntryConfChangeV2 {\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\treturn errBreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}); err != nil && err != errBreak {\n\t\tr.logger.Panicf(\"error scanning unapplied entries [%d, %d): %v\", lo, hi, err)\n\t}\n\treturn found\n}\n\n// campaign transitions the raft instance to candidate state. This must only be\n// called after verifying that this is a legitimate transition.\nfunc (r *raft) campaign(t CampaignType) {\n\tif !r.promotable() {\n\t\t// This path should not be hit (callers are supposed to check), but\n\t\t// better safe than sorry.\n\t\tr.logger.Warningf(\"%x is unpromotable; campaign() should have been called\", r.id)\n\t}\n\tvar term uint64\n\tvar voteMsg pb.MessageType\n\tif t == campaignPreElection {\n\t\tr.becomePreCandidate()\n\t\tvoteMsg = pb.MsgPreVote\n\t\t// PreVote RPCs are sent for the next term before we've incremented r.Term.\n\t\tterm = r.Term + 1\n\t} else {\n\t\tr.becomeCandidate()\n\t\tvoteMsg = pb.MsgVote\n\t\tterm = r.Term\n\t}\n\tvar ids []uint64\n\t{\n\t\tidMap := r.trk.Voters.IDs()\n\t\tids = make([]uint64, 0, len(idMap))\n\t\tfor id := range idMap {\n\t\t\tids = append(ids, id)\n\t\t}\n\t\tslices.Sort(ids)\n\t}\n\tfor _, id := range ids {\n\t\tif id == r.id {\n\t\t\t// The candidate votes for itself and should account for this self\n\t\t\t// vote once the vote has been durably persisted (since it doesn't\n\t\t\t// send a MsgVote to itself). This response message will be added to\n\t\t\t// msgsAfterAppend and delivered back to this node after the vote\n\t\t\t// has been written to stable storage.\n\t\t\tr.send(pb.Message{To: id, Term: term, Type: voteRespMsgType(voteMsg)})\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\t// TODO(pav-kv): it should be ok to simply print %+v for the lastEntryID.\n\t\tlast := r.raftLog.lastEntryID()\n\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x [logterm: %d, index: %d] sent %s request to %x at term %d\",\n\t\t\tr.id, last.term, last.index, voteMsg, id, r.Term)\n\n\t\tvar ctx []byte\n\t\tif t == campaignTransfer {\n\t\t\tctx = []byte(t)\n\t\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
