{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The controller now marks the scoped admission violation as confirmed. The campaign path has additional protections: it ignores requests from an existing leader and checks voter eligibility and pending snapshots before scanning unapplied entries. Its test advances the internal applied index without activating the configuration, so it does not independently support a stronger activation-before-campaign requirement. I also found a map error: the scan starts at `applied + 1`; it does not clamp that index to `firstIndex`.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > campaign_feedback.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v5.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\nb=next(x for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id']=='B_ELECT')\nb['implementation_guards'][-1]='hasUnappliedConfChanges returns false when applied >= committed; otherwise it scans [applied+1, committed+1) in pages for either configuration entry type. It does not clamp the lower bound to firstIndex. The internal acknowledged frontier controls this scan independently of external activation.'\nb['important_branches'].append('hup returns immediately when already leader; otherwise promotable requires local nonlearner progress and no next or in-progress snapshot before the unapplied-configuration scan. Passing the scan permits campaigning, not necessarily election victory.')\nb['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(b['source_ids']+['src_campaign_conf_test','src_nextents_test_helper']))\nfor key in ['formation','context','connection']:\n p=m['core_overview'][key]\n if 'B_ELECT' in p['behavior_ids']:p['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(p['source_ids']+b['source_ids']))\n# Keep tests local to the behavior account; the overview adds only the important guard connection.\nm['core_overview']['context']['explanation']+=' The configuration scan reads from applied+1 to committed, while existing-leader, local voter eligibility and pending-snapshot checks independently gate campaigning. A passed scan alone is not evidence that a new leader can obtain a quorum.'\nopen('campaign-map.json','w').write(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nchange={'impact':'clarification','source_ids':['src_election','src_cfg_activation','src_campaign_conf_test','src_nextents_test_helper'],'rationale':'Correct the previously overstated lower-bound clamp and retain independent campaign guards. The helper used by the campaign test advances applied without invoking configuration activation, limiting what that test establishes.','preserves':'No Fact identity, meaning or producer/consumer edge changes. The pending configuration admission check observes stepLeader, not a later campaign; B_ELECT supplies only its initial legitimate election prefix, which has no pending configuration. The self-Match explanation and storage preservation check do not rely on the incorrect clamp. Existing requirements, executed histories and scoped outcomes remain unchanged.'}\ns={'action':'research','rationale':'Retain the A2 source discriminator and correct a concrete shared-map error. Do not derive a new activation-before-campaign obligation from a test whose helper advances bookkeeping without activating configuration.','map_path':'campaign-map.json','map_changes':{'B_ELECT':change,'core_overview':change},'sources':[{'id':'src_nextents_test_helper','file':'raft_test.go','start_line':31,'end_line':44,'kind':'test_expectation'}],'feedback':{'ref_ids':['5f04338bd9e04060b57241324ec589da','e95f1065728c4e208a166729b65d273f','src_election','src_cfg_activation','src_campaign_conf_test','src_nextents_test_helper'],'answered':'The controller assessment for C_PENDING_CONFIG_ADMISSION now records outcome violated, confirmed true, bounded_complete true and reviewed_complete true with no blockers, attributed to execution 5f04338bd9e04060b57241324ec589da and review e95f1065728c4e208a166729b65d273f. That status is confined to the admission contract. The next A2 consumer was source-reviewed: hup ignores an existing leader, then requires promotability (local nonlearner progress and no pending/in-progress snapshot), then scans committed entries after applied. A failed scan blocks; a passed scan only permits campaign, whose votes and active membership still determine victory. Therefore the existing single-leader admission witness cannot simply be reused as an authority-transition witness. The campaign test first expects a follower with unapplied committed configuration to remain a follower, then calls nextEnts and permits transfer. Reading nextEnts shows direct raftLog.appliedTo after persistence and acknowledgment processing, without ApplyConfChange. This test demonstrates the internal frontier gate, not an independent guarantee that membership activation completed before campaigning. The shared map also incorrectly claimed a max(applied+1, firstIndex) scan lower bound; actual source uses applied+1, and this submission corrects it.','remaining':['No public Node follower campaign history with deferred activation has been executed here. An A2 execution would require an actual follower prefix and a distinct campaign or transfer schedule, preserving membership and vote provenance.','An independently applicable activation-before-campaign or stronger consensus obligation is not established merely by the internal scan guard or this helper-based test. The Node admission promise does not automatically transfer to this consumer.','The paused synchronous send-order wording conflict remains unresolved. The completed admission and storage checks do not decide it.'],'understanding':'updated','rationale':'Source review answered the immediate question at lower cost than another constructed election history: the candidate admission finding does not propagate to campaign safety, and the available test is weaker than an activation requirement. Repeating a known acknowledgment effect through another API would not by itself close the missing normative or quorum endpoint. Next compare the retained frontier for bounded completion versus a genuinely independent, sourced responsibility, rather than create a redundant obligation.'}}\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 campaign_feedback.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
